# A two-player battle quit from the pause screen (docs/port/QA.md 5): the race end gives each player's pending
# packet back (object_activate), then the game over screen. The packet's flag bytes follow its Link, and each
# frame's listener copy (main_menu_input) writes its vectors after them: at the N64's offsets the two wrote the
# link's prev pointer, and the unlink faulted.
# until: 0x800000:200
# seconds: 120
# expect: state=0x00800000: players 2, windows 2
5 A            # the controller pak warning
8 START        # the start prompt
9 RIGHT 0.1    # the main menu's first option: two players
11 A           # the main menu: the race
14 A           # the player screen: both ready
14 A@2
15 DOWN 0.1    # the mode screen: five modes down
15.2 DOWN 0.1
15.4 DOWN 0.1
15.6 DOWN 0.1
15.8 DOWN 0.1
17 A           # battle mode
20 A           # the track select: the battle arena
23 A           # the car select: each player's car
23 A@2
30 START       # pause
31 UP 0.1      # its last item, quit
32 A           # are you sure?
33 RIGHT 0.1   # yes
34 A           # retired: the game over screen
